    <h1>Divorce in Pennsylvania:<br>What It Means for Your <span class="brand-italic">Finances</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Pennsylvania splits support into a part with a formula and a part left to the judge, and it divides property "equitably," which is not the same as equally. Before you make decisions about your home, your support, and your retirement, here is how Pennsylvania actually handles the money, in plain language.</p>
    <p class="updated">Reviewed against Pennsylvania divorce law as of the date noted. General financial guidance, not legal advice.</p>
  </div>
